<!-- SECTION 4: WHO CAN FILE -->
<section class="content-section" id="who-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <h2 class="section-title">Who Needs Tender Turnover Certificate in Pune</h2>
            <div class="content-text">
                
                <p><strong>Civil/Infrastructure Contractors (PMC, PCMC, PWD, PMRDA):</strong> Road, drainage, building, bridge, flyover, metro, water supply, SWM. Thresholds Rs 50 lakh to Rs 50+ crore. Both total and similar works turnover. PMC follows Maharashtra PWD Manual. PMRDA mega-projects have highest thresholds.</p><p><strong>Electrical/Mechanical Contractors (MSEDCL, MSRTC, Railways):</strong> HT/LT lines, substations, streetlighting, pumping stations, HVAC, railway maintenance. MSEDCL requires turnover from "similar electrical works." Railways require specific declarations about work-in-hand.</p><p><strong>IT and Software Companies (GEM Portal, PSU Empanelment):</strong> Software development, AMC, IT infrastructure, digital transformation. GEM: "average annual turnover of at least 30% of estimated cost for last 3 years." PSU empanelment: fixed turnover thresholds.</p><p><strong>Supply and Trading Firms (PMC/PCMC Supply, GEM):</strong> Construction materials, office equipment, furniture, medical supplies. Supply tenders require total annual turnover proof. GEM: seller turnover for category registration.</p><p><strong>Manufacturing/Defence (MES, Ordnance, BEL, HAL):</strong> Defence procurement from MES Pune Garrison, Ordnance Factory Khadki. Classified turnover from defence contracts. MES formats per Manual on Contracts.</p><p><strong>MSME Units (All Categories):</strong> Udyam-registered bidders get turnover relaxation, EMD exemption, 25% reservation, 15% price preference. Still need turnover certificates - exemption applies to threshold, not certificate requirement.</p>

            </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

