                <p><strong>GFR 2017 (Rule 173):</strong> Mandates financial evaluation of bidders in government procurement. Turnover certificate is the primary prequalification document.</p><p><strong>CVC Guidelines:</strong> Transparent financial assessment in public procurement. CA-certified turnover with UDIN is the accepted standard.</p><p><strong>MSE Procurement Policy 2012:</strong> 25% procurement from MSEs. Prior turnover/experience relaxation. EMD exemption. 15% price preference.</p><p><strong>Maharashtra PWD Manual:</strong> Governs PMC, PCMC, and Maharashtra PWD tender procedures. Prescribes financial eligibility including minimum turnover.</p><p><strong>UDIN (ICAI):</strong> Mandatory since February 2019. Non-UDIN certificates rejected. Verified at udin.icai.org.</p><p><strong>E-Tender Portals:</strong> <a href="https://gem.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GEM Portal</a> | mahatenders.gov.in (Maharashtra) | eprocure.gov.in (Central) | ireps.gov.in (Railways)</p>

